{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"musophobic-secondary-jaguar","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nOn Gerrit change 1551 patchset 1, the contributor comment recheck-review was posted at 2026-08-08 22:15:03 UTC to retrigger the vote-less LLM review. The in-progress Verified run 31281019658 was then cancelled and Gerrit recorded a replacement Verified run 31281251686. The documented triggers are intentionally distinct: recheck-review queues only LLM-Review, while recheck queues only Verified.\n\n## Plan\n- Inspect the Gerrit-to-platform comment parser and dispatch path for the Verified trigger.\n- Make the recheck matcher reject recheck-review and other larger hyphenated or underscored tokens.\n- Add regression coverage for both trigger directions and preserve legitimate recheck comments.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A recheck-review comment does not cancel, reset, or dispatch a Verified run.\n- [ ] A whole-word recheck comment still dispatches the Verified workflow.\n- [ ] Regression tests cover hyphenated, underscored, prefixed, and suffixed near-misses.\n- [ ] The contributor documentation remains accurate for the two distinct self-service triggers.","id":"0d78-6c15-db26-4cea","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["gerrit","ci","retrigger"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Prevent recheck-review from retriggering CI"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786227385213896001,"uuid":"106cbf47-4e76-4997-aae4-533e57bf0131"}